---
description: Force non-fast Composer 2.5 for subagents
alwaysApply: true
---

# Subagent model: Composer 2.5 (never fast)

- NEVER pass `model: composer-2.5-fast` (or any `*-fast` Composer slug) to Task/subagents.
- When spawning a Composer-backed Task subagent, prefer the custom user subagent `composer-standard` (defined in `~/.cursor/agents/composer-standard.md` with `model: composer-2.5[fast=false]`).
- If the Task tool rejects `composer-2.5` / bracket syntax as an inline model, do NOT fall back to `composer-2.5-fast`. Omit `model` (inherit parent) or dispatch `composer-standard` by name instead.
- Bare `composer-2.5` without brackets can silently resolve to fast on some paths; rely on `composer-standard` or omit model.
